## Method
Python 3.11 with pandas, scikit-learn 1.3.0, plotly 5.17.0. Environment: gars-bio.

1. Load gene-level counts matrix (genes × samples) and design table (sample metadata).
2. Filter genes: retain only genes with ≥ 10 total reads across all 6 samples (removes ~40% of low-abundance genes that add noise).
3. Log-transform: apply log2(counts + 1) to stabilize variance across the dynamic range of expression.
4. Standardize: center each gene (subtract mean) and scale (divide by std dev) so high-abundance genes don't dominate PCA.
5. Fit PCA with scikit-learn.decomposition.PCA, extracting 3 components (n_components=3).
6. Extract PC1 and PC2 scores for each sample and output to TSV.
7. Create interactive HTML scatter plot (plotly) with:
   - X-axis: PC1, Y-axis: PC2
   - Color: treatment group (treated vs untreated)
   - Marker size/style: replicate number
   - Hover: sample ID, treatment, PC1, PC2, PC3, variance explained
8. (Optional) Export PC loadings (top 20 genes per component) to a separate TSV for interpretation of what genes drive the separation.

